solution_steps:
To evaluate the expression, we substitute $a = 1\frac{1}{2}$ into the expression.
\begin{align*} (5a^2 - 13a + 4)(2a - 3) &= \left(5\left(\frac{3}{2}\right)^2 - 13\left(\frac{3}{2}\right) + 4\right)\left(2\left(\frac{3}{2}\right) - 3\right)\\ &= \left(5\cdot\frac{9}{4} - 13\cdot\frac{3}{2} + 4\right)\left(2\cdot\frac{3}{2} - 3\right)\\ &= \left(\frac{45}{4} - \frac{39}{2} + 4\right)\left(3 - 3\right)\\ &= \left(\frac{45 - 78 + 16}{4}\right)(0)\\ &= \frac{-17}{4}(0)\\ &= \boxed{0}. \end{align*}
The answer is: 0

