We can rewrite the sum as
\begin{align*}
\sum_{n = 1}^\infty \frac{n^2 + n - 1}{(n + 2)!} &= \sum_{n = 1}^\infty \frac{n^2 + n - 1}{(n + 2)(n + 1)n!} \\
&= \sum_{n = 1}^\infty \frac{n^2 + n - 1}{(n + 2)(n + 1)} \cdot \frac{1}{n!} \\
&= \sum_{n = 1}^\infty \left( \frac{1}{n} - \frac{2}{n + 1} + \frac{1}{n + 2} \right) \cdot \frac{1}{n!}.
\end{align*}
We can now split the sum into three separate sums:
\begin{align*}
\sum_{n = 1}^\infty \left( \frac{1}{n} - \frac{2}{n + 1} + \frac{1}{n + 2} \right) \cdot \frac{1}{n!} &= \sum_{n = 1}^\infty \frac{1}{n} \cdot \frac{1}{n!} - \sum_{n = 1}^\infty \frac{2}{n + 1} \cdot \frac{1}{n!} + \sum_{n = 1}^\infty \frac{1}{n + 2} \cdot \frac{1}{n!} \\
&= \sum_{n = 1}^\infty \frac{1}{n \cdot n!} - \sum_{n = 1}^\infty \frac{2}{(n + 1) \cdot n!} + \sum_{n = 1}^\infty \frac{1}{(n + 2) \cdot n!}.
\end{align*}
Simplifying each of the three sums, we find that they telescope:
\begin{align*}
\sum_{n = 1}^\infty \frac{1}{n \cdot n!} &= \sum_{n = 1}^\infty \left( \frac{1}{n!} - \frac{1}{(n + 1)!} \right) = 1, \\
\sum_{n = 1}^\infty \frac{2}{(n + 1) \cdot n!} &= \sum_{n = 1}^\infty \left( \frac{1}{n!} - \frac{1}{(n + 1)!} \right) = 1, \\
\sum_{n = 1}^\infty \frac{1}{(n + 2) \cdot n!} &= \sum_{n = 1}^\infty \left( \frac{1}{(n + 1)!} - \frac{1}{(n + 2)!} \right) = \frac{1}{2}.
\end{align*}
Therefore, the sum is $1 - 1 + \frac{1}{2} = \boxed{\frac{1}{2}}$.
The answer is: \frac{1}{2}

