5^{-1} &\equiv 9 \pmod{11}, \\
7^{-1} &\equiv 8 \pmod{11}.
\end{align*}
Next, we add these inverses:
\begin{align*}
3^{-1} + 5^{-1} + 7^{-1} &\equiv 4 + 9 + 8 \\
&\equiv 21 \\
&\equiv 10 \pmod{11}.
\end{align*}
Finally, we take the inverse of $10$ modulo $11$ to get:
\begin{align*}
(3^{-1}+5^{-1}+7^{-1})^{-1} &\equiv 10^{-1} \\
&\equiv 10 \pmod{11}.
\end{align*}
Therefore, the remainder when $a$ is divided by $11$ is $\boxed{10}$.The answer is: 10

