dot((4.5,0. The value of the expression $5))$ is 1. What is the value of unknown variable X?

solution_steps:
First, we find the inverses of $3,$ $5,$ and $7$ modulo $11$:
\begin{align*}
3^{-1} &\equiv 4 \pmod{11}, \\
5^{-1} &\equiv 9 \pmod{11}, \\
7^{-1} &\equiv 8 \pmod{11}.
\end{align*}
Then, we add the inverses:
\begin{align*}
3^{-1} + 5^{-1} + 7^{-1} &\equiv 4 + 9 + 8 \\
&= 21 \\
&\equiv 10 \pmod{11}.
\end{align*}
Finally, we take the inverse of $10$ modulo $11$ to find $a$:
\begin{align*}
(3^{-1} + 5^{-1} + 7^{-1})^{-1} &\equiv 10^{-1} \\
&\equiv \boxed{10} \pmod{11}.
\end{align*}
The answer is: 10
